Loss (gain) on digital assets

We recognized a loss on digital assets of $21.0 thousand for the year ended December 31, 2025 as a result of a decrease in the price of bitcoin in the last quarter of 2025. The loss consisted of a $3.0 million unrealized loss on digital assets held in treasury, offset by a $3.0 million realized gain on sales of bitcoin during the year. There was a $1.4 million unrealized gain on digital assets and a $0.7 million realized gain on sales of bitcoin during the year ended December 31, 2024.

